 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "100: the Companions are praised in the tafsirs' words; no people drawn; Paradise (14-22): light only, no river. 101:14-17 «سنعذبهم مرتين» is not glossed: the tafsirs differ on the two punishments. 102: two paths for the mixed deeds, light for «عسى الله أن يتوب عليهم». STAGING v4: c1 (100): a town by day (Medina). Three believers stand on the left (the Ansar); three believers walk in from the right on 100:4 (the Muhajirun: Al-Muyassar, they left their people and moved to the abode of Islam); on 100:5 the Ansar walk to the middle of the town to meet them (As-Sa'di, quoting 59:9: they love those who emigrated to them) and the two groups stand side by side; a footsteps plate on 100:7-8 (those who followed them); a geometric plate from 100:9 to the end (Allah pleased with them, His reward; a light plate would start on His attribute). Paradise (100:14-25) is words only: the camera stays on the believers in the town, no garden, river or gold is drawn. Nobody speaks, bows or turns toward an empty side. c2 (101) stays ambient: hypocrites hidden among them, Allah tells the Messenger that he does not know them and that He will punish them twice (the tafsirs differ on the two punishments); the background is quiet over 101:12-22 (Allah's speech in the first person). c3 (102): inside a home by day; three believers (those who confessed: Medina and around it). They lower their heads on 102:2 (they admitted their sins and regretted them: both tafsirs); the two-paths plate on 102:4-5 (they mixed good with bad; it leaves before 102:6, whose spelling the name check reads as a prophet's name); they raise their hands on 102:12 (As-Sa'di: hoping that Allah forgives them; no plate over the raised hands); a geometric plate on 102:15 (Forgiving, Merciful). No pillar or mosque is drawn (no occasion of revelation is staged). Cover: the Muhajirun and the Ansar together (100:8)."
 },
